---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';

const url = 'https://barmooncontracting.com/services/general-contracting-belton-tx';

const pageSchemas = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'Service',
    serviceType: 'General Contracting',
    name: 'General Contracting in Belton, TX',
    description:
      'General contractor serving Belton and Lake Belton–area homes—repairs, renovations, painting, roofing, additions, and project management built for clay soils and storm seasons.',
    provider: { '@type': 'GeneralContractor', name: 'Bar Moon Contracting', url: 'https://barmooncontracting.com/' },
    areaServed: [
      { '@type': 'City', name: 'Belton, TX' },
      { '@type': 'AdministrativeArea', name: 'Bell County, TX' },
    ],
    url,
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://barmooncontracting.com/' },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Services', item: 'https://barmooncontracting.com/services' },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: 'General Contracting in Belton, TX', item: url },
    ],
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'FAQPage',
    mainEntity: [
      {
        '@type': 'Question',
        name: 'Do you serve all of Belton and Lake Belton areas?',
        acceptedAnswer: {
          '@type': 'Answer',
          text: 'Yes. We regularly work in Belton city limits, near Lake Belton, and on rural properties along the corridors toward Temple, Salado, and Morgan’s Point Resort.',
        },
      },
      {
        '@type': 'Question',
        name: 'How do clay soils around Belton affect renovations?',
        acceptedAnswer: {
          '@type': 'Answer',
          text: 'Expansive clay can shift foundations, slabs, and exterior hardscape. We plan drainage, pier/footing details, and material choices with that movement in mind so repairs and additions last longer.',
        },
      },
      {
        '@type': 'Question',
        name: 'Can you handle storm damage and insurance work in Belton?',
        acceptedAnswer: {
          '@type': 'Answer',
          text: 'Yes. We document damage, work with adjusters when needed, and coordinate roofing, interior repairs, and related trades under one project plan.',
        },
      },
      {
        '@type': 'Question',
        name: 'How long does a typical Belton project take?',
        acceptedAnswer: {
          '@type': 'Answer',
          text: 'Small repairs: 1–5 days. Larger remodels or additions: often 2–6 weeks depending on scope, permits, and material lead times. We give a written timeline before work starts.',
        },
      },
    ],
  },
];
---

<Layout
  title="General Contracting in Belton, TX | Bar Moon Contracting"
  description="Belton general contractor for repairs, renovations, painting, roofing, and additions—planned for Lake Belton weather, clay soils, and clear project management."
  schemas={pageSchemas}
>
  <Header />

  <main class="pt-20 bg-light-neutral text-primary">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 py-20">
      <div class="mb-8 text-sm text-gray-600">
        <a href="/services" class="text-accent hover:underline">Services</a>
        <span class="mx-2">/</span>
        <span>General Contracting in Belton, TX</span>
      </div>

      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold mb-6">General Contracting in Belton, TX</h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-700 mb-10">
        Belton homeowners need a contractor who understands lake-adjacent weather, older housing stock, and the
        clay soils that run under much of Bell County. Bar Moon Contracting is your single point of contact for
        repairs, renovations, painting, roofing, additions, and full project coordination—without the runaround.
      </p>

      <div class="prose max-w-none text-gray-700 mb-16 space-y-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl">Why Belton projects are different</h2>
        <p>
          Belton sits between Temple’s medical corridor and the recreation draw of Lake Belton and Belton Lake
          Outdoor Recreation Area. That mix shows up in the housing: mid-century ranch homes near downtown and
          the university area, newer subdivisions pushing toward the loop, and lake-proximate properties where
          humidity, drainage, and wind-driven rain matter as much as looks. A generic “Central Texas” bid that
          ignores those conditions often underestimates site work, exterior detailing, and weather delays.
        </p>
        <p>
          We plan Belton jobs with expansive clay, seasonal storms, and real family schedules in mind. That means
          honest scopes, written change-order processes, and material choices that hold up when the ground moves
          and summer heat bakes exterior finishes. Whether you are near Nolan Creek, off FM corridors, or on a
          quieter rural lot toward Holland or Little River, we start with a walkthrough—not a one-size quote.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl">What we handle for Belton homeowners</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>General repairs and maintenance for occupied homes and small commercial spaces</li>
          <li>Painting, roofing, and exterior finish work suited to sun and storm exposure</li>
          <li>Storm damage restoration and insurance-claim documentation support</li>
          <li>Kitchen and bath remodels, additions, and multi-trade renovations</li>
          <li>Coordination of electrical, plumbing, HVAC, and specialty trades</li>
          <li>Church, facility, and light commercial projects when a GC is needed</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl">Local conditions we plan for</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Clay and drainage.</strong> Much of the Belton area sits on expansive soils that swell when wet
          and shrink when dry. That movement can open cracks in slabs, affect patio attachments, and stress
          exterior transitions. We look at grading, downspouts, and how new work ties into existing structures
          before we break ground.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Heat and humidity.</strong> Lake influence and Central Texas summers punish cheap paint systems,
          poorly ventilated baths, and outdoor structures without proper detailing. We specify finishes and
          ventilation that match how Belton homes are actually lived in—not brochure climates.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Permits and inspections.</strong> City of Belton and Bell County requirements differ by scope
          and location. We handle permitting and inspections for compliant work so you are not chasing paperwork
          between jobsites and city counters.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl">Our process in Belton</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>
            <strong>Consultation</strong> — We meet on site (or by phone first if that fits your schedule) to
            understand the problem, budget range, and any hard deadlines.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Assessment &amp; plan</strong> — Measurements, photos, and a written plan that accounts for
            soil, access, and trade sequencing.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Transparent proposal</strong> — Clear scope, pricing, and a realistic timeline before work
            starts—no vague “we’ll see” line items.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Execution</strong> — Supervised work, clean jobsite habits, and updates as phases complete.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Walkthrough</strong> — We do not call it done until you walk the job with us and issues are
            closed.
          </li>
        </ol>

        <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl">Belton FAQs</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Do you serve all of Belton and Lake Belton areas?</strong> Yes. We regularly work in Belton city
          limits, near Lake Belton, and on rural properties along the corridors toward Temple, Salado, and
          Morgan’s Point Resort.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>How do clay soils around Belton affect renovations?</strong> Expansive clay can shift
          foundations, slabs, and exterior hardscape. We plan drainage, pier/footing details, and material choices
          with that movement in mind so repairs and additions last longer.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Can you handle storm damage and insurance work in Belton?</strong> Yes. We document damage, work
          with adjusters when needed, and coordinate roofing, interior repairs, and related trades under one
          project plan.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>How long does a typical Belton project take?</strong> Small repairs: 1–5 days. Larger remodels
          or additions: often 2–6 weeks depending on scope, permits, and material lead times. We give a written
          timeline before work starts.
        </p>

        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
          Also serving nearby:{' '}
          <a href="/services/general-contracting-temple-tx" class="text-accent hover:underline">Temple general contracting</a>
          {' · '}
          <a href="/services/general-contracting-harker-heights-tx" class="text-accent hover:underline"
            >Harker Heights general contracting</a
          >
          {' · '}
          <a href="/service-areas" class="text-accent hover:underline">All service areas</a>
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-deep-blue text-white p-8 rounded-2xl">
        <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">Need a general contractor in Belton?</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-white/90">Clear scope, honest pricing, and craftsmanship built for Bell County conditions.</p>
        <a href="/get-quote" class="inline-block bg-accent hover:bg-gold text-dark-blue font-bold px-8 py-3 rounded-lg"
          >Get a Free Quote</a
        >
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm">
          Call or text: <a href="tel:2545813808" class="text-gold-primary">(254) 581-3808</a> · Mon–Fri 8:00 AM –
          6:00 PM
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
